WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.672
This rehearsal joins the school Week Five requirements into a sequence you can explain and practise. It does not add another hidden module or substitute a set of disconnected textbook facts for the weekend.
本演练把学校第5周要求连成能解释及练习的顺序，不新增隐藏模块，也不用分散教材事实取代周末课程。

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:28.872
Saturday centers on the arrest team, shockable and nonshockable rhythms, CO2 change, ROSC and resuscitation decisions. Sunday moves into the deteriorating cardiac patient, timed ECG, perfusion and live notification.
周六核心是骤停团队、可电击与不可电击心律、CO2变化、ROSC及复苏决策；周日转向恶化心脏患者、限时ECG、灌注及现场通知。

00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:41.304
Use a manikin, training device or spoken tabletop exercise as appropriate. This course cannot certify physical compression quality, device fit or a clinical skill from a screen alone.
可依条件使用人体模型、训练设备或口头桌面演练。仅看屏幕不能由本课程认证真实按压质量、器械适配或临床技能。

00:00:41.304 --> 00:00:52.536
Practise the original scenarios here, not a school quiz or an answer key. The purpose is to make the reasoning and teamwork executable before the actual supervised class.
应练这里原创情境，不打开学校测验或答案。目的是让推理及合作在真实监督课堂前能执行。

00:00:52.536 --> 00:01:06.600
Use AP and cardiovascular pathophysiology to explain the pump, rhythm and serial circuit. CNS and MSN connect those mechanisms to the focused assessment, shock and the nitrate-preload problem.
用AP及心血管病理生理解释泵、心律和串联循环；CNS及MSN把机制连到重点评估、休克及硝酸酯前负荷问题。

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:19.800
Use BCEHS for the named service pathways and BCPEG for the saved examination-guide wording. They are not always identical, and a school page reference does not prove which revision will govern a future assessment.
BCEHS对应具名机构路径，BCPEG对应保存的考试指南措辞；二者不总相同，学校页码也不证明未来考核采用哪版。

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:38.712
FON, CPSC and VSM support team behavior, focused observations and safe practical delivery. PHARM explains the drug mechanisms and risks, while PMHN provides the ethical concepts relevant to patient wishes and difficult resuscitation conversations.
FON、CPSC及VSM支持团队行为、重点观察及安全实操；PHARM解释药物机制风险，PMHN提供患者意愿及困难复苏沟通所需伦理概念。

00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:53.424
Nancy remains the supplied main examination text, integrated through the weekly topics. The eleven assigned reading rows all have bilingual guides, but unresolved edition and linked-activity gaps are not marked fully certified.
Nancy仍是已提供主考教材，并按周主题整合。十一项指定阅读均有中英指南，但未解决版本及链接活动缺口不会标成完整认证。

00:01:53.424 --> 00:02:05.976
Name who is leading, compressing, managing the airway and operating the monitor. Add treatment, recording and communication roles as staff arrive, matching tasks to actual capability.
需明确谁带队、按压、管气道及操作监护。人员增加后加入治疗、记录和沟通角色，任务与真实能力对应。

00:02:05.976 --> 00:02:17.424
The leader states the immediate goal and prepares the next transition before it happens. Everyone should know the next planned rhythm assessment, compressor exchange and relevant safety check.
带队者说清即时目标，并在转换前准备。所有人应知道下一计划心律评估、按压者交换及相关安全核查。

00:02:17.424 --> 00:02:30.960
Use a directed instruction, acknowledgement and completion report. A read-back is useful communication, but it does not replace observing a real all-clear or independently checking a calculation when required.
应指名下令、确认及报告完成。回读有助沟通，但不能替代真正观察已清场，也不能替代规定独立药算核查。

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:43.440
Maintain shared awareness of the patient, not only individual tasks. Anyone who sees ineffective care, a hazard or a major patient change should state it clearly and receive a response.
团队共同关注患者，而不只各做各的。任何人发现无效照护、危险或重大患者变化，都应明确提出并得到回应。

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:56.664
With limited personnel, prioritize the effective initial arrest response and use available help. Do not create an elaborate six-person role plan before compressions and the usable AED pathway begin.
人员少时先保障有效初始骤停响应并使用可用帮助，不能在按压及可用AED流程前先花时间编六人复杂分工。

00:02:56.664 --> 00:03:10.848
As resources arrive, transfer tasks explicitly: who takes over, what has happened and what must continue. A working airway or defibrillation setup should not disappear because someone assumed another person had it.
资源到后，要明确谁接手、发生了什么及必须继续什么。不能因各自以为别人负责，就让有效气道或除颤设置丢失。

00:03:10.848 --> 00:03:23.640
Prepare an equipment exchange before removing a working device. A new monitor or mechanical compressor is not inherently more valuable than uninterrupted effective treatment already in progress.
应在撤掉有效设备前准备替代。新监护仪或机械按压器，并不天然比正在进行的不中断有效治疗更重要。

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:35.760
The team structure can change while the clinical goal stays consistent. Review any avoidable no-treatment interval afterward and identify its exact cause rather than blaming the number of people.
团队结构可变，临床目标应一致。事后检查本可避免的无治疗间隔及确切原因，不能只怪人多人少。

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:52.416
On the adult manikin, practise the trained compression target of one hundred to one hundred twenty per minute, approximately five to six centimeters deep, with full recoil. Device feedback or a displayed rate is useful but not the entire quality assessment.
成人模型练习受训目标：每分钟100至120次，约5至6厘米，完全回弹。反馈器或显示频率有帮助，但不是全部质量评估。

00:03:52.416 --> 00:04:05.736
Use the appropriate ventilation strategy for the actual airway and workflow. Avoid excessive rate or volume and check chest movement and the team’s timing instead of squeezing a full bag on every breath.
应按实际气道及流程采用适当通气策略，避免过快过大；要查胸廓运动和团队时序，不是每次都挤完整气囊。

00:04:05.736 --> 00:04:19.344
Plan necessary pauses and keep them as short as possible; a ten-second upper bound is not a desired pause length. Count the actual interruption, including an unplanned delay before compressions resume.
必要停顿应预先计划并尽量短；十秒上界不是目标停顿长度。计时要含恢复按压前未计划延误。

00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:31.992
If the manikin reports a problem, change one specific action and measure again. A subjective feeling of good CPR or a successful story ending cannot certify the underlying performance.
模型反馈有问题时，应改变一个具体动作再测。主观觉得CPR很好或故事结局成功，不能认证真实表现。

00:04:31.992 --> 00:04:43.968
Begin the drill during ongoing CPR and announce the coming assessment. Prepare the actual authorized monitor mode, connections and energy without adding avoidable interruption.
演练从持续CPR开始并宣布将评估。准备真实获授权模式、接头及能量，不增加可避免停顿。

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:55.128
Interpret the rhythm during a reliable brief assessment. Compression artifact is not a reason to guess a shockable pattern, and a charged device does not create an indication.
应在可靠短评估中解释心律。按压伪差不能成为猜可电击模式的理由，器械充能也不会创造指征。

00:04:55.128 --> 00:05:07.296
Perform the actual all-clear rather than merely saying a phrase. Include patient contact, surrounding hazards and the specific oxygen arrangement under the trained device workflow.
需要真正清场，不能只说一句话。按受训器械流程核患者接触、周围危险及具体供氧安排。

00:05:07.296 --> 00:05:19.800
After an indicated shock, promptly resume useful CPR through the correct workflow. Do not add a routine immediate postshock pulse hunt or stand watching the screen to see whether the story improved.
有指征电击后，应依正确流程迅速恢复有效CPR。不能额外常规马上找脉，或站着盯屏幕等故事好转。

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:31.608
Change the scenario to organized electrical activity without effective circulation. That is not a reason to shock merely because the QRS looks dramatic or the device is charged.
把情境改为有组织电活动却无有效循环。不能因为QRS看着明显或已充能就电击。

00:05:31.608 --> 00:05:43.560
Announce the nonshockable decision, disarm safely if necessary and resume the appropriate CPR and ventilation sequence. Preserve the clinical reason and time in the record.
应宣布不可电击决定，必要时安全撤能，并恢复适当CPR及通气，记录临床理由及时间。

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:54.000
Look for plausible reversible causes using the patient’s context and observations. Do not spend a prolonged pause listing causes while no one compresses.
按患者背景及观察寻找可信可逆病因，不能在无人按压时长停顿背病因。

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:05.616
An AED no-shock message does not prove effective circulation or authorize stopping resuscitation. Reassess the actual patient and follow the appropriate arrest decision pathway.
AED不建议电击，不证明有效循环，也不授权停复苏。需重评实际患者并遵循适当骤停决策路径。

00:06:05.616 --> 00:06:20.328
Recall the full school Hs and Ts framework, then attach evidence. Hypoxia, hypovolemia, hydrogen-ion disturbance, potassium disturbance and hypothermia are not diagnosed merely by naming them.
先回忆完整学校Hs及Ts，再连证据。低氧、低血容量、氢离子、钾及低温问题，不会因说出名字就确诊。

00:06:20.328 --> 00:06:34.320
The T group includes tension pneumothorax, tamponade, toxins and pulmonary or coronary thrombosis. Several mechanisms can coexist; an arrest rhythm alone does not identify which one is present.
T组包括张力气胸、压塞、毒物及肺或冠脉血栓，多种可并存，骤停心律本身不能确定哪项存在。

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:50.712
Assign a focused question or examination while effective arrest care continues. A history of fluid loss, a disconnected airway or a relevant medication exposure can direct a specific correction more usefully than an unprioritized list.
有效骤停照护继续时，可分配重点提问检查。失液史、气道脱接或相关药物暴露，比无优先级清单更能指向具体纠正。

00:06:50.712 --> 00:07:04.008
Some definitive treatments require advanced or specialized resources. Recognizing the possibility helps escalation, but does not grant an untrained operator permission to perform an invasive procedure.
部分确定性治疗需高级或专门资源，识别可能性有助升级，但不授权未受训者做侵入操作。

00:07:04.008 --> 00:07:17.688
Start with a real repeated waveform and understand the sampling interface. CO2 must be produced, carried to the lungs, exhaled and sampled, so a number can change for more than one reason.
先确认真实重复波形并理解采样接口。CO2需产生、运到肺、呼出及采到，所以数字可因多种原因变化。

00:07:17.688 --> 00:07:31.224
For a low or falling value, check actual ventilation, airway, sampling and compression performance in context. Do not automatically ventilate faster or assume the patient is beyond help.
低值或下降时，应结合背景核实际通气、气道、采样及按压表现，不能自动加快通气，也不能认定没救。

00:07:31.224 --> 00:07:46.344
The school emphasizes a sudden sustained rise as a major ROSC clue. Communicate it and assess circulation appropriately without an unnecessary prolonged pause; confirm the transition rather than declaring it from one number.
学校强调突然持续升高是重要ROSC线索。需通报并适当评循环，不额外长停顿，确认转换而非凭单值宣布。

00:07:46.344 --> 00:08:00.960
For resuscitation decisions, isolated ETCO2 is not a stand-alone termination test, particularly with nonintubated sampling. Keep the actual pathway, clinical evidence and consultation requirements together.
复苏决策中，孤立ETCO2不是单独终止检验，非插管采样尤其如此。需把真实路径、临床证据及咨询要求一起用。

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:14.208
Once evidence supports ROSC, announce the new state so the whole team changes the plan together. Compressions-generated pulses or an organized trace alone cannot establish the transition.
证据支持ROSC后，要宣布新状态，让全队一起改计划。按压产生的脉或有组织记录本身不能确立转换。

00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:28.608
Reassess airway, breathing, circulation and consciousness. Provide the indicated support and prepare for recurrent deterioration; the resuscitation is not finished because one cycle ended with a pulse.
需重评气道、呼吸、循环及意识，给有指征支持并准备再恶化，不会因一个周期结束时有脉搏就完成复苏。

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:48.048
Titrate oxygen when reliable measurements and the applicable pathway permit, and avoid excessive ventilation. The current N Zero Three page, its older checklist and the AHA comparison have numerical differences documented in the preceding lesson; do not fabricate a blended target.
可靠测量及适用路径允许时滴定氧气，并避免过度通气。现行N03、较旧清单及AHA比较中的数字差异已在前课标明，不能混造目标。

00:08:48.048 --> 00:09:03.552
Obtain the appropriate ECG and cause assessment, coordinate the receiving pathway and maintain repeated observations. Do not replace this with indiscriminate cold fluids or a universal prognosis from the early neurologic examination.
需适当ECG及病因评估、协调接收路径并维持复测，不能改成无差别冷液或凭早期神经检查给通用预后。

00:09:03.552 --> 00:09:15.168
Distinguish not starting CPR, stopping CPR after it has begun and the subsequent recognition-of-life-extinct process. They are related but not interchangeable decisions.
要区分不开始CPR、开始后停止CPR，以及随后的确认生命已逝过程，三者相关但不是同一决定。

00:09:15.168 --> 00:09:32.088
Use the actual R Zero Two criteria card from the prior lecture. Rapid, twenty-minute and thirty-or-forty-minute pathways have conditions and minimums, not automatic stop alarms. A prior brief ROSC or a shockable period can change a branch.
应使用前课真实R02条件卡。快速、二十分钟及三十或四十分钟路径都有条件及最低时长，不是自动停表。之前短暂ROSC或可电击时期，都可改变分支。

00:09:32.088 --> 00:09:47.064
Prepare the required early consultation with true no-flow, CPR, rhythm, shocks, ROSC, causes and patient-wish information. Do not wait until a timer expires to discover that the important history is missing.
需以真实无血流、CPR、心律、电击、ROSC、病因及患者意愿信息准备规定早期咨询，不能等时钟结束才发现关键史没问。

00:09:47.064 --> 00:10:02.592
After an authorized discontinuation, use the actual ROLE process and required paired observations. A fixed pupil, family preference, isolated CO2 value or classroom minimum alone does not replace that process.
获授权终止后，需用真实ROLE流程及规定共同观察。瞳孔固定、家属偏好、孤立CO2或课堂最低时长，都不能替代。

00:10:02.592 --> 00:10:15.360
Use clear, compassionate language and identify who can communicate while the clinical team continues care. Do not make promises about survival or imply that a single monitor value determines the outcome.
应清楚、体恤地沟通，并明确临床照护继续时由谁沟通。不能保证存活，也不能暗示一个监护值决定结局。

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:30.000
Ask about known wishes and relevant documents without treating every relative as the automatic decision-maker. Apply the actual legal and clinical process, including clarification when documents or accounts conflict.
应问已知意愿及相关文件，但不能把每位亲属当自动决定人。需用真实法律及临床程序，文件或说法冲突时要澄清。

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:42.360
If resuscitation ends through the authorized process, state the reality plainly and allow questions. Do not use vague phrases that leave the family believing treatment has merely paused.
若经获授权程序结束复苏，应平实说明现实并允许提问，不能含糊到让家属以为只是暂时停治疗。

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:57.888
Respect privacy and dignity, explain practical next steps through the appropriate service and document important communication factually. Ethical principles guide the process; they do not provide blanket immunity or unilateral TOR authority.
需尊重隐私尊严，通过适当机构说明实际下一步，并如实记重要沟通。伦理原则指导流程，不提供普遍免责或单方停复苏权。

00:10:57.888 --> 00:11:11.808
The school names a LUCAS station, while the current public service procedure allocates mechanical CPR to advanced crews and selected medical-arrest situations. Learning the station does not erase that operational boundary.
学校点名LUCAS实操站，而现行公开机构流程分配机械CPR给高级团队及特定内科骤停情境。学习该站不会抹去操作边界。

00:11:11.808 --> 00:11:25.992
Use the actual trained device version and IFU. Prepare components and a manual fallback, apply the correct landmarks and height without precompression, and verify the state and fit rather than forcing the frame.
需用真实受训机型及说明书，备组件和手动备用，正确定位高度且不预压，并核状态适配，不能硬压框。

00:11:25.992 --> 00:11:39.144
Preserve manual compressions whenever possible during preparation and keep the necessary application interruption short. A supposedly flawless machine is not a reason to stop checking effective care.
准备时尽可能维持手动按压，必要安装停顿尽量短。不能因觉得机器完美就不再核有效照护。

00:11:39.144 --> 00:11:53.208
After attachment or movement, recheck position, mode, actual compression performance and airway/ventilation. A correctly named mode alone cannot prove the cup is still in the correct place.
装好或移动后，应重查位置、模式、实际按压及气道通气。模式名称正确，本身不能证明杯仍在正确位置。

00:11:53.208 --> 00:12:05.592
Introduce an unsafe fit or a simulated fault. The expected response is prompt effective manual CPR and safe device management, not a long discussion while compressions are absent.
可引入不安全适配或模拟故障，预期反应是迅速有效手动CPR及安全器械管理，不是无按压地长讨论。

00:12:05.592 --> 00:12:19.320
For the planned battery change, the reviewed IFU preserves the position within its specified interval and returns from PAUSE to PAUSE. The sixty-second memory is not permission for a sixty-second CPR interruption.
计划换电时，已审说明书在规定区间保留位置，从PAUSE开始则回PAUSE。六十秒记忆不是允许CPR停六十秒。

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:33.336
Verify the state and patient before restarting. Use the trained rhythm-analysis and defibrillation workflow rather than assuming mechanical motion cannot create artifact or that every procedure requires the same pause.
重启前需核状态及患者。应依受训心律分析和除颤流程，不能假设机械运动无伪差，也不能假设每个操作停法一样。

00:12:33.336 --> 00:12:46.656
After ROSC, do not apply a universal retain-the-frame rule from a school claim. Patient access, breathing, comfort, position, readiness and local instruction must inform the plan.
ROSC后，不能照学校一句话通用保留框。患者接近、呼吸、舒适、体位、再准备及本地指令均需参与计划。

00:12:46.656 --> 00:12:58.992
The technical goal is a useful recording, while the clinical goal is to preserve necessary care. Divide tasks so speed does not come from ignoring the patient or guessing electrode positions.
技术目标是有用记录，临床目标是保持必要照护。要分工，速度不能靠忽略患者或猜电极位置。

00:12:58.992 --> 00:13:11.256
Use the verified Week Three contact-to-readable clock as a carryover practice target. Week Five requests timed acquisition, but an unrecovered separate grading rule is not invented.
可用核实的第3周接触至可读时钟作为延续练习目标。第5周要求限时采集，但不会编造未取得的另一评分规则。

00:13:11.256 --> 00:13:23.112
Check patient identity, actual standard lead positions, artifact and the symptom state. Label additional right-sided or posterior views distinctly through the trained pathway.
需核身份、真实标准位置、伪差及症状状态，受训路径下额外右侧或后壁记录要分别标明。

00:13:23.112 --> 00:13:33.456
Record the start, usable finish and reason for delay. Practise the specific weak link again instead of simply trying to move faster through every action.
应记开始、可用完成及延迟原因，再专练薄弱点，不是所有动作都盲目加速。

00:13:33.456 --> 00:13:44.832
Identify the inferior leads as a group and relate the pattern to symptoms. Do not claim that the same artery or right-ventricular physiology is proven in every patient.
应成组识别下壁导联并连症状，不能声称每位患者都已证明同一动脉或右室生理。

00:13:44.832 --> 00:13:57.912
State the pressure, rate and perfusion rather than simply saying inferior means no nitrate. The school hypotensive, bradycardic presentation already fails important current screening conditions.
要说血压、心率及灌注，而不只是说下壁就不许硝酸酯。学校低血压慢心率表现，本身已不符合重要现行条件。

00:13:57.912 --> 00:14:12.144
Ask the relevant medication and volume questions and consider right-sided involvement. Explain how additional venodilation could reduce serial flow and why a fluid bolus is not an automatic opposite answer.
需问相关药物及容量问题、考虑右侧受累，并解释额外静脉舒张怎样减少串联血流，以及为何反过来推液也不自动正确。

00:14:12.144 --> 00:14:26.280
Describe the positive care plan after withholding: support threats, obtain appropriate resources, reassess and coordinate the receiving pathway. Safe exclusion must lead to useful care, not paralysis.
不做后要说明积极照护计划：支持威胁、取适当资源、复评及协调接收。安全排除应导向有效照护，而不是不敢行动。

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:35.424
Open with the time-critical working problem and the patient’s current state. The receiving team needs more than the words possible cardiac patient.
开头应是有时效的工作问题及当前患者状态，接收团队需要的不只是可能心脏患者。

00:14:35.424 --> 00:14:51.288
Give the important times, ECG territory and perfusion trend. Report uncertainty honestly, including an unknown onset or artifact limitation, rather than making the message sound complete by inventing a fact.
给重要时间、ECG区域及灌注趋势，未知起病或伪差限制应诚实说，不能为消息完整而编事实。

00:14:51.288 --> 00:15:04.416
State what treatment occurred and the response, including an important withheld nitrate and its reason. Request or confirm the actual regional pathway rather than promising universal ED bypass.
说明实际治疗及反应，包括重要未给硝酸酯及理由。应请求确认真实区域路径，不能保证普遍绕过急诊。

00:15:04.416 --> 00:15:16.392
Finish with arrival time, support needs and confirmation of receipt or the next step. Then continue patient care; a polished radio message does not guarantee a stable journey.
结尾给抵达时间、支援需要及接收确认或下一步，之后继续照护，漂亮无线电消息不保证途中稳定。

00:15:16.392 --> 00:15:28.392
Take one example from this week: ASA one hundred sixty versus one hundred sixty-two, or the three different atropine starting doses in Nancy, PHARM and the checked local monograph.
从本周挑一例：ASA 160与162，或Nancy、PHARM及核对的本地专论中三个不同阿托品首剂。

00:15:28.392 --> 00:15:41.880
Name the source and context first. Do not average doses, combine repeat schedules or select the most permissive number. An educational advanced-dose comparison is not independent PCP authority.
先点来源背景，不能平均剂量、合并重复方案或挑最宽松数字。高级剂量教学比较，不是PCP独立权限。

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:53.184
Explain the physiological purpose and relevant harm. This lets you understand why the discrepancy matters instead of storing two unexplained numbers that can be confused under stress.
应解释生理目的及相关损害，才能明白差异重要处，而非只存两个无解释、压力下会混的数字。

00:15:53.184 --> 00:16:05.664
For an actual school assessment or clinical procedure, obtain the governing version and instruction through the correct channel. A course production gap remains visible until that evidence is obtained.
真实学校考核或临床操作，应通过正确渠道取得适用版本及指令；课程制作缺口在证据取得前保持可见。

00:16:05.664 --> 00:16:18.312
In a training calculation, one milligram divided by point-one milligram per milliliter equals ten milliliters. The units cancel to volume, which is why concentration must be explicit.
训练计算中，1 mg除以0.1 mg/mL等于10 mL，单位约成体积，所以必须明确浓度。

00:16:18.312 --> 00:16:30.648
The same mass from one milligram per milliliter occupies one milliliter. This arithmetic difference does not make the two products or routes interchangeable, and it is not a patient-specific order.
同一质量若来自1 mg/mL则是1 mL。算术差异不表示两制剂或途径可互换，也不是患者特定医嘱。

00:16:30.648 --> 00:16:44.808
For a weight-based infusion, retain kilograms, micrograms, minutes and hours until the expression ends in milliliters per hour. Check device precision and the maximum or titration instruction before measuring.
按体重输注时，应保留kg、mcg、分钟及小时，直到表达式变mL/h。测量前需查器械精度及最大量或滴定指令。

00:16:44.808 --> 00:16:57.720
Then check indication, contraindications, route, rate, order and operator authority. An independently correct calculation can still describe an unsafe or unauthorized treatment.
之后还需核指征、禁忌、途径、速度、医嘱及操作者权限。独立算对也仍可能是不安全或越权治疗。

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:09.888
Begin with a community-workshop collapse, bystander CPR and a working AED. Assign roles and preserve the usable care while learning the reported collapse and no-flow history.
从社区工作坊倒下、旁观者CPR及可用AED开始，分角色并维持可用照护，同时了解报告的倒下及无血流史。

00:17:09.888 --> 00:17:22.872
Now introduce a cable fault in the replacement monitor. Assign focused troubleshooting while the existing CPR and AED workflow continue; do not remove the working treatment to make room for a broken replacement.
再引入替代监护仪线缆故障。应指派针对排查，其余现有CPR及AED继续，不能为坏替代品腾地方撤掉有效治疗。

00:17:22.872 --> 00:17:35.664
Later introduce a sustained CO2 rise. The team must communicate, check the patient appropriately and confirm whether the transition is real, then use the correct subsequent pathway.
之后引入CO2持续升高，团队需沟通、适当查患者并确认转换是否真实，再用正确后续路径。

00:17:35.664 --> 00:17:50.040
Run a second version with no ROSC and prepare an evidence-based consultation without inventing an ending. Success is coherent care and a defensible decision process, not forcing every scenario to survive.
第二版不发生ROSC，需准备有证据咨询而不编结局。成功是连贯照护及可说明决策过程，不是硬让每个情境存活。

00:17:50.040 --> 00:18:01.584
Start with the original chest-symptom patient from the previous lecture. State the working problem, screen treatment, prepare a useful ECG and begin the time-sensitive pre-alert.
从前课原创胸部症状患者开始，说明工作问题、筛治疗、准备有用ECG并启动有时效预警。

00:18:01.584 --> 00:18:13.992
Change only ventilation to inadequate while a pulse remains. The team must notice, announce and respond rather than continuing a medication discussion or automatically choosing CPAP.
只把通气改为不足，脉搏仍有。团队需发现、宣布及响应，不能继续药物讨论或自动选CPAP。

00:18:13.992 --> 00:18:25.920
Then remove effective circulation. Announce the arrest and allocate CPR, ventilation and the appropriate analysis workflow, preserving what remains useful from the existing setup.
再使有效循环消失，需宣布骤停、分配CPR、通气及适当分析，并保留原有设置中仍有用部分。

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:39.168
If the drill later produces confirmed ROSC, announce it and change the whole plan again. The recorder and communicator must update the current state, not keep reporting the initial presentation.
若后来练习中确认ROSC，需宣布并再次改整套计划，记录及沟通也更新当前状态，不能还只报最初表现。

00:18:39.168 --> 00:18:51.744
Record true times and distinguish observation from witness report or estimate. No-flow before CPR and low-flow during CPR are different intervals and may affect later decisions.
需记真实时间并区分观察、目击报告和估计。CPR前无血流与CPR中低血流是不同区间，可影响后续决定。

00:18:51.744 --> 00:19:03.528
Reconcile device events with the actual clinical record. Not every drug, pulse check, conversation or human decision is automatically captured, and device clocks can differ.
需把器械事件与真实临床记录核对。不是每次药物、查脉、对话或决定都会自动捕获，设备时钟也可能不同。

00:19:03.528 --> 00:19:17.064
Document actual interventions and response, consultation facts and direction, exclusions and unresolved uncertainty. Do not chart an action as completed merely because it was planned or ordered.
要记实际干预及反应、咨询事实和指令、排除及不确定性，不能只因计划或下令就记已完成。

00:19:17.064 --> 00:19:29.880
Handover the current patient and required ongoing support using the trained structure. Confirm transfer of responsibility; the record is for continuity of care, not a promise of immunity.
需按受训结构交接当前患者及仍需支持，并确认责任转移。记录用于照护连续，不保证免责。

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:41.880
Review what actually happened before discussing what should have happened. Use the interruption clock, manikin feedback, trace quality, communication and record to identify a specific gap.
复盘先看实际发生，再谈应该发生。可用停顿计时、模型反馈、记录质量、沟通及病历定位具体缺口。

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:54.432
Do not judge the whole team by ROSC alone or attribute every problem to an individual. Consider setup, roles, environment, device compatibility and the information available at the time.
不能只按ROSC评价团队，也不能每个问题都怪个人。需考虑准备、角色、环境、器械相容及当时可用信息。

00:19:54.432 --> 00:20:07.656
Choose one change: prepare a connector earlier, name the next compressor before the pause, or include the withheld-nitrate reason in the radio message. Repeat the same drill to see whether the change helped.
选一个改变：更早备接头、停前点名下一按压者，或无线电加入未给硝酸酯原因。再做同一练习，看改变是否有用。

00:20:07.656 --> 00:20:20.064
Separate operational review from personal psychological support. Offer appropriate voluntary support without forcing traumatic disclosure or pretending a learning discussion eliminates accountability.
操作复盘与个人心理支持要区分。可提供适当自愿支持，不能强迫创伤披露，也不能假装学习讨论取消责任。

00:20:20.064 --> 00:20:31.848
You should now be able to explain why each action belongs in the sequence, not merely recite a checklist. Link physiology, patient findings, treatment choice and reassessment.
现在应能解释每项行动为何在顺序中，而不只是背清单，要连接生理、患者发现、治疗选择及复评。

00:20:31.848 --> 00:20:45.480
Practical readiness also requires supervised performance on the actual equipment and patient-appropriate technique. Watching a lecture and passing an original practice question cannot establish that by itself.
实操准备还需要监督下在真实器械上用适当技术演示，观看讲座及答对原创题本身无法建立。

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:56.904
Keep exact school-edition and missing-PowerPoint or rubric gaps visible. The course does not mark an unseen requirement complete or present this rehearsal as a school-assessed pass.
确切学校版本、缺原幻灯片或评分表应保持可见，课程不会把未见要求标完成，也不会把演练说成学校考核通过。

00:20:56.904 --> 00:21:08.904
Use the original review questions to identify what to repeat, then continue into the next school week. The final whole-course package is withheld until content and delivery checks are complete.
可用原创复习题定位需重练部分，再进入学校下一周。整套最终包要到内容及交付检查完成后才制作。
